	(text "FujiNet for the Nintendo Entertainment System - Rev0 (RP2354B)\n\nRP2354B (48 GPIO) sits on the 5V cart bus directly through its 5V-tolerant pads: CPU A0-A14, D0-D7, M2, R/W,\n/ROMSEL, PPU A10-A12 in; /IRQ out; it serves $5000-$7FFF and the reset vectors itself and drives the two\nAS6C4008 SRAMs' bank lines (PRG A13-A18 = GP33-38, CHR A10-A18 = GP39-47) from PIO lookup tables.\nThe SRAMs and the 74HCT glue run on +5V (console 5V / USB VBUS diode-OR) so their outputs drive the 5V bus.\n74HCT595 holds the slow control bits (SRAM_EN PRG_WE_EN CHR_WE_EN MIR0 MIR1 FOURSCREEN LED spare);\n74HCT253 muxes CIRAM A10 for mirroring; PWR_OK (console +5V sense) gates every output toward the console.\nESP32-S3-WROOM-1-N16R8 runs FujiNet (fujiversal-nes) and is the USB host of the RP (CDC, VID 0xCafe);\nS3 IO4/IO5 force RP RUN/QSPI_SS so the S3 can re-flash the RP over PICOBOOT.\nUSB-C: power + CP2102N UART bridge for flashing the S3.  microSD on S3 SPI.\nEdge: 72 pins, 2.50 mm pitch, 1-36 on the label side (nesdev Cartridge connector page). EXP, CIC, SYSTEM CLK unconnected."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
